I, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",["O"]="Bring a pair of Legplates of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.",["T"]="Anthion's Parting Words",},[26263]={["D"]="Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\
\
The only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\
\
I, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!",["O"]="Bring a pair of Legplates of Valor to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.",["T"]="Anthion's Parting Words",},[26264]={["D"]="I have jobs available for contractors willing to assemble a team. Time to make the magic of the holidays! Here's one from the holiday decor division.\
\
Contract #1010: Obtain Magical Residue from within Baradin Hold\
\
Quantity: Four Samples",["O"]="Collect 4 Vials of Magical Residue from Baradin Hold.",["T"]="Contract #1010: Magical Residue",},[26265]={["D"]="Hail $C! I could use your assistance.\
\
The dry heat of the desert is parching person and beast alike. I've heard that the Kirin Tor at Tol Barad may have a special way of conjuring the most refreshing crystal water. Would you be willing to make the journey there and see if you could learn how this is done so you could restock our supplies?",["O"]="Learn how to conjure Crystal Water from someone in Baradin Hold, then bring 20 Conjured Crystal Water to Nalaeth Lunabranch at Valor's Rest in Silithus.",["T"]="Arcane Refreshment",},[26266]={["D"]="You're with the Horde, right? I'm looking to join a faction, and I think it's the obvious choice, all things considered...\
\
Morgria and her caravan ran into me here at my camp. When we each explained why we're here, well... it's a match made in the twisting nether -- would you believe our goals completely align? So, we've tentatively agreed: I provide intelligence on Felstone Fortress and a remedy to this curse going around, in exchange for citizenship in the Horde.\
\
Regarding the curse, I have a plan that may or may not pan out. It's no permanent solution, but I can try to give the Horde a bit of a reprieve. That is -- as long as I have some help only a $C can provide.\
\
I need tomes from the cultists near here, specifically the ones that practice magic or rituals. Thugs and enforcers won't do. The thicker the tome, the better. I'll explain more when I have them.",["O"]="Collect 8 Shadowsworn Tomes from cult members in the wastes of the Blasted Lands.",["T"]="Dark Literature",},[26267]={["D"]="<Izalnir hunches over, scanning the grimoire's pages with his milky eyes for a long time. Eventually, he looks up at you.>\
\
Have you come across anything that looks like this? Something written on a scroll, or perhaps even a stone?\
\
<Izalnir shows you a page filled with chaotic script encircling a wicked looking rune.>\
\
The warlocks are using these to play around with the curse -- the balefire -- in ways I didn't think possible. Ha, the fools are even using it for alchemy.\
\
I'll need one of these glyphs if we're to continue, and I don't imagine anyone but Felstone's warlocks would have anything like this. The fortress is too dangerous alone, so bring friends. I'll read on until you're back.",["O"]="Obtain a Glyph of Affliction from the warlocks inside Felstone Fortress.",["T"]="Reverse Affliction",},[26268]={["D"]="See the glyph's inscription here? It's inked in kuzhir atramentum: very potent, and very hard to get, even for warlocks. Demon blood is the main component of the ink, giving it a black sheen that devours light.\
\
Hmm... the lexicon they're using originates from Argus Wake circles abroad. I can read it enough to make my own adjustments, but I don't have any atramentum of my own.\
\
<Izalnir looks to you with an expectant grin.>\
\
Would you get some, please? Warlocks and their acolytes have them. I'd wager you'll find it in warlock tents around the fortress. The huts may have some as well.",["O"]="Collect 5 Kuzhir Atramentum Vials from around Felstone Fortress.",["T"]="Rewriting Curses",},[26269]={["D"]="What did you feel when you held this glyph? Nausea? An itch that couldn't be scratched?\
\
<Izalnir lays a hand on the rune and closes his eyes.>\
\
For me, it's a thumping on my head. Like... someone rattling their cage. I've heard of powerful soulstones smuggled out of some cave in the back of Felstone... it's no small jump to assume that's how our glyph here was charged.\
\
The orcs inside that hollow are on another level, not deigning to associate with anyone else. That said, sometimes theft, trade, or a simple mistake leads to one of their coveted stones ending up where it shouldn't.\
\
Maybe you've already seen some? I need at least one for my plan to bear fruit. The warlocks around Felstone probably have some.\
\
If you're feeling foolhardy, you could also try the cave itself. It's west of Felstone's center, with giant bones wreathing the entrance. I've never been inside, but I've heard stories...",["O"]="Find 1 Grombolar Soulstone for Izalnir from the corpses of cultists within Felstone Fortress.",["T"]="Soul Fuel",},[26270]={["D"]="Time for our final act. Your group is familiar with Felstone's dangers now, so hopefully this won't be too difficult.\
\
The plan is this: take the revised glyph to the altar on the highest terrace of southern Felstone and use it on the ritual circle. It's a purple rune radiating dark magic. In theory, this glyph will rip the curse away from its targets and return it to the ritual circle -- no permanent solution, as I said.\
\
I don't know the consequences of doing this, so be prepared for anything. Good luck, $N.",["O"]="Use the Altered Glyph of Affliction on the ritual circle at the high altar on Felstone's uppermost terrace to the far south.",["T"]="Distant Disruption",},[26271]={["D"]="Hello there, hope you're liking Winterspring! I love the dry air, coming from Darkshore's gloom. You're an adventurer, right?\
\
I'm a student jeweler, here for those pretty crystals all around the area. Rumor has it they fall from the sky -- it's probably where the village get its name from! The tools I brought with me won't shape them, though. Believe me, I tried! My finest grinder broke...!\
\
These crystals aren't something new, so surely the ancient highborne had some way of cutting them, right? I'll pay for anything you can find! Kel'theril is to the south, and... Teles'aran is northeast of here, but there's a mean old lady on the road leading there.",["O"]="Eleanor Moonglow at Starfall Village wants you to recover a Highborne Artisan Kit from one of the larger highborne ruins in Winterspring.",["T"]="Ancient Gemcutting",},[26272]={["D"]="Hmm... this kit is really old... I don't feel comfortable using it just yet.\
\
<Eleanor scratches her brow, inspecting the artisan kit with a surprisingly keen eye.>\
\
Oh, I know! I met a goblin in Everlook and loaned him some supplies. He's an engineer and owes me a favor! Are you headed that way? Would you mind dropping this off with him? Just tell him I sent you and that I'd be grateful to have it restored.",["O"]="Deliver the Highborne Artisan Kit to Felnok Steelspring in Everlook.",["T"]="We Need Repairs!",},[26273]={["D"]="This is exciting, $N! I can't wait to start making jewelry. I'm sure Felnok's a good engineer, but it'd be a challenge for anyone restoring relics that old.\
\
In the meantime, why don't we gather as many crystals as we can find? I'll make you a piece of jewelry when all's said and done! Does that sound fair?",["O"]="Eleanor Moonglow at Starfall Village wants you to gather 10 Starfall Crystals from around Winterspring.",["T"]="Falling Stars",},[26274]={["D"]="Alright, $N. I'd go with you to pick up the kit, but I don't feel comfortable leaving all these jewels alone... what if someone stole them?\
\
I'm sorry to lean on you so much. I'll make it up to you, I promise! No, I'm not lazy!",["O"]="Pick up the Restored Artisan Kit from Felnok Steelspring in Everlook and return to Eleanor Moonglow in Starfall Village in Winterspring.",["T"]="Felnok's Finesse",},[26275]={["D"]="<Eleanor warily attempts to shape one of the crystals.>\
\
Huh... maybe I'll get Felnok to come by and explain what all this extra stuff is for. Thankfully, the tools are working well, so I'll shape your gemstone now!\
\
It shouldn't take long! There's a bag of settings inside that crate in the house behind me. Would you do one last thing and bring me the bag? Please?!",["O"]="Bring Eleanor the Bag of Gem Settings from the crate inside the house behind her.",["T"]="A Gift, For You!",},[26276]={["D"]="We're still working on an efficient way to drill into Gnomeregan and begin repairing the damage to the city. What we need is more power! \
\
I have a cousin who got a job working at some lab in Blackrock Depths. They're building golems there that are powered by obsidian cores. I'd like to examine one of those cores to see if it would work for me. \
\
My cousin mentioned there's an older golem named Phalanx who uses an obsidian core. It's due to be decommissioned -- so no one should miss it if you can obtain its core!",["O"]="Retrieve an Obsidian Core from Phalanx in Blackrock Depths for Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.",["T"]="Operation: Phalanx",},[26277]={["D"]="My responsibilities with the Earthen Ring include monitoring the use -- and misuse -- of fire energy by shamans. Recently I felt a jarringly strong pull of fire from far away -- Blackrock Mountain. \
\
I believe a former member of the Earthen Ring has taken up with the Dark Iron dwarves who dwell in the depths of the mountain and is experimenting with mixing fire elemental energy that shamans use and the arcane fire magic used by mages. \
\
Such a perversion of the elements must be stopped. I am needed here to continue my research in primordial magic -- but perhaps you and a few comrades could take care of this rogue shaman. \
\
His name is Tonaka Loregrain.",["O"]="Kill Pyromancer Loregrain in Blackrock Depths, then return to Yaluni Flamewatcher at Marshal's Refuge in Un'Goro Crater.",["T"]="Shaman of the Flame",},[26278]={["D"]="You have shown me that you can defeat our enemies and perform missions to further the cause of the Waterlords. But until now you have only faced lesser foes... it is time you undertook missions of greater skill and danger. \
\
Within the depths of Blackrock Mountain the Dark Iron dwarves conspire with the Firelord's servants. Slay two of his chief emissaries: Lord Roccor and Ambassador Flamelash. \
\
Do this and prove to me your dedication to our cause.",["O"]="Slay Lord Roccor and Ambassador Flamelash in Blackrock Depths, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",["T"]="The Firelord's Lieutenants",},[26279]={["D"]="Captain Winky is a sore loser. SORE I SAY! \
\
Winky said the Dark Iron Dwarves had the good stuff but I said NO! There must be something better. \
\
And I heard there is. \
\
And it's called Mag. Ma. \
\
Mag. Ma. \
\
Mag. Mus. Magmus! Kill it! Maybe not with fire though.",["O"]="Kill Magmus deep within Blackrock Depths, then return to Oralius at Morgan's Vigil in the Burning Steppes.",["T"]="The Gooder Stuff",},[26280]={["D"]="Well I never! $N, I'm sorry to say that I need the help of an adventurer like ye. \
\
I've just learned that one o' my former students has been spotted training demon dogs in Blackrock Depths. He should be killin' demons, nae consortin' with 'em! \
\
I wish to rescind the diploma I awarded to 'im -- Grebmar is his name -- but we Ironforge dwarves are nae welcome in the Dark Iron city. Can ye deliver the bad news and retrieve the diploma?",["O"]="Slay Houndmaster Grebmar and retrieve his Hunter School Diploma for Ulfir Ironbeard in Stormwind.",["T"]="The Wayward Student",},[26281]={["D"]="Upon examining the ember, you notice it feels alive, pulsing in your hand. You recall hearing that Gakin the Darkbinder has experience dealing with strange objects like this, and may be able to investigate further.\
\
You can find him in The Slaughtered Lamb, located in The Mage Quarter of Stormwind.",["O"]="Bring the Eternal Ember to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.",["T"]="An Eternal Flame",},[26282]={["D"]="You look like the enterprising type willing to take a job without asking too many questions. Just the type I've been looking for.\
\
Before I settled down here in Springsocket I used to have my own business moving goods from one place to another. Back then I had a \"partner\" who helped... smoothe out the rough edges of customs and paperwork. Then the Venture Co. came in and recruited them out from under me, and the whole operation fell apart. I was stranded here in the desert!\
\
Even though things worked out, a goblin doesn't forget that kind of grudge. I gotta stay here to mind my enterprise, but if you're willing to pay Supervisor Grimgash in Glittermurk Mines a visit, I'd be very happy to reward you.",["O"]="Locate Supervisor Grimgash within Glittermurk Mines and slay him.",["T"]="An Old Debt",},[26283]={["D"]="Before you is an old and weathered idol vaguely in the shape of an unfathomably ancient human. This may be of interest to a knowledgeable Historian -- the most notable of which can be found in the Ironforge Hall of Explorers.",["O"]="Locate a knowledgeable Historian within Ironforge.",["T"]="Azothan Relic",},[26284]={["D"]="It is stated that thousands of years ago the trolls warred with a group known only as the Azotha. Very little is known about them, however some of our more eccentric curators, including myself, believe there is much more here than meets the eye.\
\
If what you've said is true and the Venture Co. have stumbled on a cache of their artifacts, it is imperative that you bring them to me. They belong in a museum! Would you delve into their mine and collect as many as you can for me?",["O"]="Collect Azothan Relics within Glittermurk Mines.",["T"]="Azothan Relics",},[26285]={["D"]="What's a life without a few vices, eh $C?\
\
Sadly, I haven't been able to smoke my favorite pipe since I lost it when I was out on the beach east of town. I was a bit 'o sheets to the wind, if ya catch my drift, and when I came to my senses, I saw a big murloc making off with it!\
\
Seems that murloc's made a home up in Glittermurk Mines. If you happen up that way and you get a chance to grab my pipe, I'd be real grateful.",["O"]="Recover Deeg's Lost Pipe from Murklurk within Glittermurk Mines and bring it to him in Booty Bay.",["T"]="Deeg's Lost Pipe",},[26286]={["D"]="The Venture Co. have a whole damned mining complex up there! No wonder I'm struggling to get ahold of any Singing Crystals. An operation of that size has a good chance to make the foundations of the jungle crumble. Someone is going to have to deal with it before it gets out of hand!\
\
Do me a favor, go take out the competition and bring me the head of the Glittermurk Mines Foreman. With him gone, not only can I start to make some tidy profit around here, but the jungle won't be destroyed in the process!",["O"]="Slay the Venture Co. Foreman within Glittermurk Mines.",["T"]="Kill the Foreman",},[26287]={["D"]="Since you were so helpful in fulfilling my order for the Excelsior line of boots, I think you should help me with my experimental new design.\
\
I'm expanding beyond crocolisk skins into basilisk -- but not just any basilisk. I want only the best. I hear the Venture Co. found a big, shiny, special basilisk in Glittermurk Mines. That's the one I need. Head out there and bring me its scales!",["O"]="Collect Prismatic Scales from a basilisk inside Glittermurk Mines and bring them to Drizzlik in Booty Bay.",["T"]="Prismatic Scales",},[26288]={["D"]="So here's the deal $N -- a few months back I was commissioned to craft some high quality tools for a certain operation being undertaken within Stranglethorn. The foreman called it Glitter... something. Glittermurk!\
\
I don't know what they were digging up, but they threw manpower at the mine, and gold at supplying the miners with tools.\
\
Since then, I've received a much much more profitable commission right here in Tanaris, and I need every tool I can get back to fill the order.\
\
If you keep this between me and you, I think you can go and \"recover\" the tools I made from the Glittermurk miners and everyone is happy. Well, minus the Glittermurk chumps, haha. Whaddya say?",["O"]="Recover 20 tools from the Venture Co. within Glittermurk Mines.",["T"]="Reclaiming Tools",},[26289]={["D"]="As a long-time servant of my queen, I abhor disloyalty. Yet, errant naga lose their way when lead by corrupted servants of the deep.\
\
You like little errands, don't you, mortal? How about this: travel across the sea to where goblins dig. It is a place deep inland, where it is too dry to venture ourselves. The goblins have stumbled into a lair of wayward naga who are lead by the one they call Gnash. Kill Gnash's servants and then end his existence.\
\
For we can suffer none who defy the queen to live.",["O"]="Slay 5 Tidewater Oracles, 5 Tidewater Warriors, and Gnash inside Glittermurk Mines.",["T"]="Renegade Naga",},[26290]={["D"]="Before you is an old and weathered idol vaguely in the shape of an unfathomably ancient human. This may be of interest to a knowledgeable troll Lorespeaker -- the most notable of which can be found in the Orgrimmar Valley of Spirits.",["O"]="Locate a knowledgeable Lorespeaker within Orgrimmar.",["T"]="Troll Relic",},[26291]={["D"]="De legends say that thousands of years ago de trolls warred with a group known only as de Azotha. Very little is known about dem besides their tenacity in battle. I believe dere is much more here than meets de eye.\
\
If what ya said is true and de Venture Co. have stumbled on a cache of their artifacts it is imperative that you bring them to me. Would you delve into their mine and collect as many as you can for me?",["O"]="Collect Troll Relics within Glittermurk Mines.",["T"]="Troll Relics",},[26292]={["D"]="I know it's unusual for an elf, but I adore the sea. I've spent many an hour floating in the shallows east of Booty Bay, making friends with the fish and the birds. I never once felt afraid... until recently.\
\
I was floating father north than I usually do, when some great mysterious tendril reached up from the seafloor and grabbed my leg! The creature tried to pull me into an underwater tunnel, but I fought back. Finally, it released me and disappeared into the tunnel... which collapsed behind it.\
\
I think the creature might be living in that excavation the Venture Co. set up in the hills north of town. I tried to warn them but they ignored me. Please, if you enter those mines, look out for the monster! I dread anyone else encountering it unawares.",["O"]="Search Glittermurk Mines for the monster Aliss Tideseeker described and destroy it.",["T"]="Tunnel Monster",},[26293]={["D"]="You don't look too busy... how about a little task? I've been sent here by the Steamwheedle Cartel to hedge on a little bet. Gluk here thinks that one day he's going to be King Gordok, just like his father was before him, but the current King branded him as a traitor and expelled him from Dire Maul. We think Gluk has what it takes to be king... with some help from friends.\
\
I plan to forge a mighty weapon for Gluk that he can use in the coming battle, and you are going to get me all the parts I need. Deal?\
\
The first thing I need is a special type of magical wood that you can find on the Forest Walkers nearby. It's light but as strong as any metal, and will make a fine handle.",["O"]="Collect Walker Branches from Wandering Forest Walkers throughout Feralas.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26294]={["D"]="Around these parts there grows a special type of hemp that I can use to create a very strong rope. This will ensure that even if the King loses his grip, he won't lose his weapon!\
\
Ogres are strange. Rumor has it that Gluk's father, the previous King, smoked a bushel of this stuff and wandered away from his throne. As soon as he was out of sight of the ogres, they just proclaimed a new King, thus ending Gluk's claim to the throne.\
\
Anyway, the hemp grows close to the rivers in Feralas, and can be found all over the forest.",["O"]="Collect 8 bushels of Wetland Hemp for Viggo at Gluk's Compound.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26295]={["D"]="An important part of my plan requires heavily refined iron interspersed with a special alloy that you'll collect for me later. However, iron is very hard to come by in these parts!\
\
I have a bit of a workaround though: I don't need much, so we can extract it from beasts right here in Feralas.\
\
Here is a little gadget I call the Hemovac Max. Weaken a beast and slurp the iron in their blood right out of them! With enough vials I will have enough iron to work with. Sadly, since each vial has such a small quantity, it's time for a good old-fashioned wildlife massacre.",["O"]="Collect 20 Vials of Beast Blood from weakened beasts in Feralas.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26296]={["D"]="And now on to the... less pleasant stuff. There's a reason I waited until you felt invested to ask you for this. Southeast of here you will find the Writhing Deep. It's home to the skittering beasts that some have taken to calling Silithid.\
\
It is well known that sometimes they mistake ore for food and coat it with a sticky ooze. Do you know what happens when they fully consume and... pass... it?\
\
Well, what we get is a mismatch of ores that somehow form a new alloy. Don't ask me how; I've never wanted to inspect the insides of one to find out. All I care about is you getting me those alloys for Gluk's new weapon.",["O"]="Collect 12 chunks of Silithid Alloy from the Writhing Deep in Feralas.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26297]={["D"]="We're not far from being able to finally craft this kingly weapon. The bottleneck now is simple: making and maintaining the heat. The forge here is well suited for churning out the standard low quality fare the ogres typically enjoy using, but it's not hot enough to smelt these alloys and combine them with the iron.\
\
Unfortunately this means that the heat has to come to us. Far to the east, in the Eastern Kingdoms, you will find the Searing Gorge.\
\
It's the kind of place where lava flows, rock melts, and elementals run wild. I need you to collect their fiery essences and bring them to me.\
\
With those essences I can beef up this forge to handle our demands.",["O"]="Collect Swirling Molten Rock and Blistering Flame Essence from earth and fire elementals within the Searing Gorge.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26298]={["D"]="Heat is only one half of this equation $C. We need to be able to temper the flames and manage the heat, slowly allowing the alloys to melt, fuse and become something wholly new. You're in luck that I won't have to send you far to get what we need.\
\
Right on the coast of Feralas you will find water elementals that have been soaking up the cooling essence of the sea itself. Go and collect as much of it as you can, and we will use it during the forging process to avoid torching the whole compound!",["O"]="Collect Salted Cooling Essence from water elementals on the coast of Feralas.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26299]={["D"]="Right, scratch the idea of you having an easy day. There's only one place I've heard of that may have what we need: the centaur birthplace known as Maraudon.\
\
Deep within the orange caverns you will find an extremely powerful water elemental called \"Noxxion\", whose essence will serve as a far more worthy reagent for a weapon as powerful as this.\
\
Will you risk your life and your limbs in getting his essence for me? I promise, this will all pay off once Gluk rules in Dire Maul!",["O"]="Enter Maraudon and slay Noxxion. Collect his essence to bring to Viggo in Feralas.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26300]={["D"]="These two lumbering oafs behind me are Dee and Dum. They're far from smart, but they're great at whacking an anvil with a great big hammer, so as far as I'm concerned, they're as intelligent as the average blacksmith.\
\
While they forge the weapon, and suffer under the heat, I'll need you to calm the flames and cool them down with the essence from Noxxion. Don't let the ogres overheat or this will have all been for naught.",["O"]="Cool down Dee and Dum while they forge Gluk's new weapon.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26301]={["D"]="It's time to present this weapon of champions to Gluk. Would you do the honors for me?\
\
He's in the nearby cave.",["O"]="Deliver Gluk's new weapon.",["T"]="Fit For A King",},[26302]={["D"]="Oral history says that these lands were once lush, but the unleashing of the centaur by Princess Theradras within Maraudon caused a calamity that created the land we see all around us. My aim is to restore these lands with the assistance of Dibi and Kelly here.\
\
One key component we need to investigate further is a sample of the Princess herself. Not only will slaying her end further corruption, but by studying her closely we may be able to reverse it.\
\
Delve into Maraudon on my behalf and retrieve a sample for me, please. I will pay you handsomely.",["O"]="Collect a sample of Princess Theradras within Maraudon for Selrai Dewlight at Squigglecord Outpost.",["T"]="The Source Of Corruption",},[26303]={["D"]="Oh look, it's $N. I've seen you pass me by before, oblivious to the uniqueness of this place. Not two paces from where I stand is a stable tear through reality leading deep into the heart of Blackrock Mountain, to a place known as the Molten Core. This is place of great evil but also great glory for adventuresome folk such as yourself. Would you like to see it? \
\
Of course you would, but it's far too dangerous for a mortal like you to venture there without assistance. Fortunately, I am here to give you a push in the right direction. \
\
Seek out the Hydraxian Waterlords that dwell along the coast of Azshara. They have a vested interest in your success.",["O"]="Seek out Duke Hydraxis on an island off the coast of Azshara.",["T"]="Attunement to the Core",},[26304]={["D"]="The Molten Core is the lair of our mortal enemies, the elementals of fire. If left unchecked, they will grow in power until they set all Azeroth aflame. \
\
The raging center of the mountain is too hot even for the Firelord's Dark Iron allies. But, if you do my bidding, I shall grant you a boon that allows you to withstand the intense heat at the heart of the volcano. \
\
First I will need elemental materials to consume in the ritual. Gather an elemental fire, and an elemental water, some Firebloom, and some Winter's Bite. If you can't find these things in the world yourself, I believe mortals offer them for sale at some kind of trading hub.",["O"]="Bring 5 Firebloom, 5 Wintersbite, an Elemental Fire, and an Elemental Water to Duke Hydraxis on an island off the coast of Azshara.",["T"]="Attunement to the Core",},[26305]={["D"]="Next we will need the infused essences of powerful beings aligned with fire and ice. \
\
Near the Altar of Storms in Burning Steppes you will find Torid in a waterfall of lava. It is a boon to the world to slay him and retrieve his fiery core. \
\
As for frost, you will need to slay my cousin Keenice in Winterspring. He dwells along the frozen waterfall south of Lake Kel'Theril. \
\
This is an unfortunate but necessary sacrifice.",["O"]="Bring Torid's Fiery Core and Keenice's Frozen Core to Duke Hydraxis on an island off the coast of Azshara.",["T"]="Attunement to the Core",},[26306]={["D"]="Now you must gather the reagents to attune to the heat of the mountain. We will need samples of heat and resonance from the Molten Core itself -- or as close as you can safely achieve. \
\
Enter the stronghold of the Dark Iron dwarves known as Blackrock Depths. Make your way to the very bottom and you shall find their smelting station. Fill this Insulated Vial with the blistering lava nearby. \
\
Then make your way across the bridge towards the Core and collect a fragment from the nearby wall. \
\
Make no mistake mortal, this is a dangerous task, one you will not want to complete alone. Return to me afterwards, if you survive.",["O"]="Fill the Insulated Vial with the lava that flows near the entrance to the Molten Core in Blackrock Depths, and collect a Core Fragment from the wall nearby.",["T"]="Attunement to the Core",},[26307]={["D"]="I shall use the components you have gathered to empower you with my blessing. It will protect you in the Molten Core only, as it is tuned to the unique resonance of the mountain. \
\
Hold fast mortal! This may burn a little but it is a necessary evil if you are to survive delving into the very heart of Blackrock Mountain.",["O"]="Hold still while Duke Hydraxis imbues you with a charm of protection that allows you to safely enter the Molten Core.",["T"]="Attunement to the Core",},[26308]={["D"]="Well met, $C $N. I recently journeyed to the Undercity and had a chance to speak to the Fallen Knight.\
\
<The Paladin chuckles.>\
\
I would like to know her real name one day, it feels so unprofessional to refer to her as thus. Nevertheless, she spoke highly of your potential, and wanted me to send you to her to undergo some trials. Venture forth to the Undercity, and seek her out.",["O"]="Speak to The Fallen Knight in Undercity.",["T"]="Trial of the Willing",},[26309]={["D"]="I am not who I once was, $C $N. A knight of the Silver Hand, a paladin of great virtue. A defender of truth and justice. Now I lay here in the bowels of the Undercity, fishing for sickly creatures in this slime.\
\
You however, you show the willingness to battle the darkness despite said darkness resting in your own soul. I wish to trial you, if you accept.",["O"]="Speak to The Fallen Knight in Undercity if you wish to undergo the trials.",["T"]="Trial of the Willing",},[26310]={["D"]="For your first trial you will need to journey far into the northeast of Tirisfal Glades. It is east of the Scarlet Monastery, but be careful not to get too close to the Monastery, as you are not yet strong enough for that place. You should find a small stone path leading to a graveyard.\
\
At that graveyard you will find three Paladin ghosts. In life they worked together as a team, and in death they were buried in their own resting place. I sense they still cling to this world. Go and release them, so they may finally rest.",["O"]="Defeat the three ghosts of former Paladins located in the graveyard east of the Scarlet Monastery. Return to The Fallen Knight in the Undercity when you have put the spirits to rest.",["T"]="Trial of the Willing",},[26311]={["D"]="Now it is time to construct a hammer worthy of a Paladin. I know of a good smith in Orgrimmar: his name is Aturk the Anvil. Bring him this letter of specifications and payment, and he will provide you with a list of materials you will need to gather for him. You'll find him by the Blacksmithing trainers in the Valley of Honor.\
\
In the times of my life I would request a craft from Ironforge, but I have a feeling they might not accept the request nowadays.",["O"]="Deliver the letter and payment to Aturk the Anvil in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",["T"]="Materials of the Light",},[26312]={["D"]="I spend my time honing my skill and learning about materials I can play with. In my travels I have become aware of some resources that will be of use for your mace. \
\
<Aturk snaps toward Ox and tells him to write his requests down.>\
\
Take this letter, and fetch!",["O"]="Using Aturk's Material List, find some Blessed Ingots, Zelemar's Hammer, a Silver Hand Medallion, and a Kor Gem. Bring them to Aturk the Anvil in Orgrimmar.",["T"]="Materials of the Light",},[26313]={["D"]="Aturk is impressed with himself, this is a fine weapon. Fit for a strong member of the Horde! Serve us well, $N, for you are talented.\
\
I am not sorry that I doubted you, such doubts give you the drive to prove yourself! Aka'Magosh!",["O"]="",["T"]="Weapon of the Light",},[26314]={["D"]="Hail $N. Might I ask a personal favor of you?\
\
Long before the Third War I had a close personal relationship with Jandice Barov, a conjuror of no small talent. When the Scourge army descended on Lordaeron, some of my personal effects were left in Jandice's possession. Considering the circumstances under which we parted company, I do not wish to face her wrath again.\
\
But your mastery of the arcane arts rivals my own and I believe you could stand toe to toe with her. If you were willing to retrieve my Notes on Arcane Refreshment from her, I would be delighted to share the contents of said notes with you. I think you'll find the Ritual of Refreshment to be quite a time-saver!\
\
You and your companions can find Janice Barov in the basement of the Scholomance in Western Plaguelands.",["O"]="Kill Jandice Barov in the Scholomance, and retrieve High Sorcerer Andromath's Notes on Arcane Refreshment.",["T"]="Ritual of Refreshment",},[26315]={["D"]="Greetings, $N. You've grown powerful in your training and I believe there isn't much left for me to teach you. I wager you're tired of conjuring food and drinks for your allies yes? If I am correct I think you should speak to High Sorcerer Andrometh in Stormwind. I believe he knows a better way.",["O"]="Speak to High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind's Mage Quarter",["T"]="Ritual of Refreshment",},[26316]={["D"]="In life I was a legal scholar and in death I'd like to continue these studies even while I explore much broader topics. I don't have time to go out and source books from the ruins of Lordaeron, but I bet you do.\
\
Bring me these specific tomes from the ruins of Stratholme and the school of Scholomance and I'll be able to balance my Lorespeaker duties with my personal interests.",["O"]="Locate books on Lordaeron's legal practices in Scholomance and Stratholme for Lorespeaker Ebonlocke in the Undercity.",["T"]="Lorderon's Legal Legacy",},[26317]={["D"]="The Atal'ai trolls that dwell within de sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar in de Swamp of Sorrows are said to hold two ancient tablets I would like to study.\
\
Considerin' they'd kill me before I'd even get to ask, I need an adventurin' sort to head down and retrieve them. Interested in de job?",["O"]="Collect the Tablet of Alani and the Tablet of Jakari from the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",["T"]="Atal'ai Tablets",},[26318]={["D"]="Seekin' work mon? I need a brave soul to journey down south to de swamp.\
\
In de Sunken Temple you'll find High Priests and Witch Doctors. Dese trolls carry scrolls on which they be writin' de crazed prophecies of de Blood God Hakkar himself. I be keepin' an eye on his followers and dese scrolls would help me do that. Whatcha say?",["O"]="Collect 4 Atal'ai Scrolls from Atal'ai Witch Doctors and Atal'ai High Priests in the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",["T"]="Invocation of The Blood God",},[26319]={["D"]="Traveler, forgive this interruption but your name has made the circuit of the House of Nobles and I have been waiting for a hero of renown to visit the keep.\
\
With both Quel'thalas and Dalaran fallen, much of the knowledge of my people has been lost. However, the Kirin Tor maintained a library at the prison stronghold of Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad. There are a number of tomes that may be kept in the prison that I would dearly like to preserve.\
\
Could I prevail upon you to assist me in this endeavor? You would be well rewarded.",["O"]="Travel to Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad and search for the books Caledra Dawnbreeze is interested in recovering.",["T"]="A Legacy of Knowledge",},[26320]={["D"]="Traveler, forgive this interruption but your name has made the circuit of the Elders and I have been waiting for a hero of renown to visit the Spirit Rise.\
\
With both Quel'thalas and Dalaran fallen, much of the knowledge of the high elf people has been lost. However, the Kirin Tor maintained a library at the prison stronghold of Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad. There are a number of tomes that may be kept in the prison that I would dearly like to preserve.\
\
Could I prevail upon you to assist me in this endeavor? You would be well rewarded.",["O"]="Travel to Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad and search for the books Lorespeaker Ashmane is interested in recovering.",["T"]="A Legacy of Knowledge",},[26321]={["D"]="You -- yes you! Adventurer! Maybe you will listen to me!\
\
I've been petitioning various powerful people in Stormwind Keep for weeks but they won't give my request any attention. My family used to live on Tol Barad island before the Second War. Most of them died there, but an uncle of mine escaped. Before he died, he told me that a precious family heirloom was hidden in a safe place on the island. But now there's a rumor that pirates showed up at Tol Barad! They're after the treasure, I just know it.\
\
Look, $C, I'm desperate for someone to go out to the island and recover that treasure. Take this key! It will open the compartment where the treasure is hidden. Please, restore my family's legacy to me!",["O"]="Recover Rebecca Martin's lost family heirloom from the island of Tol Barad.",["T"]="An Unfinished Task",},[26322]={["D"]="The key you were given doesn't seem to open the small lockbox inside the hidden compartment. All you can do is take the lockbox back to Rebecca Martin and hope it contains the treasure she is looking for.",["O"]="Return the lost heirloom to Rebecca Martin in Stormwind.",["T"]="An Unfinished Task",},[26323]={["D"]="You -- yes you! Adventurer! Maybe you will listen to me!\
\
I've been petitioning various powerful people in the Undercity for weeks but they won't give my request any attention. My family used to live on Tol Barad island before the Second War. Most of them died there, but an uncle of mine escaped. Before he died, he told me that a precious family heirloom was hidden in a safe place on the island. But now there's a rumor that pirates showed up at Tol Barad! They're after the treasure, I just know it.\
\
Look, $C, I'm desperate for someone to go out to the island and recover that treasure. Take this key! It will open the compartment where the treasure is hidden. Please, restore my family's legacy to me!",["O"]="Recover Georgiana Martin's lost family heirloom from the island of Tol Barad.",["T"]="An Unfinished Task",},[26324]={["D"]="The key you were given doesn't seem to open the small lockbox inside the hidden compartment. All you can do is take the lockbox back to Georgiana Martin and hope it contains the treasure she is looking for.",["O"]="Return the lost heirloom to Georgiana Martin in the Undercity.",["T"]="An Unfinished Task",},[26325]={["D"]="This non-descript pile of earth doesn't seem to conceal any treasure. As you root around in the loose dirt, your fingers seem to seize on the edge of a chest before the sensation disappears.\
\
Perhaps you need specialized equipment to unearth the chest?",["O"]="Find the right tool to dig up the dirt pile you found.|cFF42E8F3\
Prerequisites:\
- Interact with Captain's Log, Volume III, located behind Pirate Lord Blackstone in Baradin Hold, while you have the effect of the potion Pirate's Parley\
- Bring a Spectral Shovel from Augustus the Touched or buy one from the Auction House|r",["T"]="Buried Treasure",},[26326]={["D"]="Among the treasures in Captain Blackstone's chest is a strange milky white orb that pulses with ominous red light. As you handle its smooth surface, the orb feels oddly reassuring. It might be wise to find out more about what this item is.",["O"]="Speak to someone who can tell you more about the Ominous White Orb.",["T"]="Into Purgatory",},[26327]={["D"]="$C, you are now bound to an Eye of Paleth cursed by stronger magic than that which holds the residents of this island in purgatory - and we were bound by the Light for our role in the abuse of those in Southshore's internment camps.\
\
It is no accident Captain Blackstone chose this island to hide his treasure. He suffered for years before he was recruited into Southshore's privateer fleet. It was a fitting task that we guard his treasure as part of our atonement. This story should have had naught to do with you, but you are deep in it now. If you don't want his mistakes to take over your life, you'll have to unravel the curse as Blackstone failed to do.\
\
I know none of the details regarding how the Eye came to be in Blackstone's possession, but I believe you'll have to trace it back to its source to break the curse that binds it to you. Blackstone came to this island with three members of his crew. Seek them out if you do not wish to succumb to madness, as Blackstone did.",["O"]="Locate Captain Blackstone's former crew members and learn what they have to say about the Eye of Paleth's origin.",["T"]="Into Purgatory",},[26328]={["D"]="So the three crew members said the treasure was in Feralas in a cave populated by naga?\
\
I do not know anything about Kalimdor to advise you further, but if you search the seaside caves of that land, I have no doubt you will find what you seek.\
\
And get another one of those shovels you used to dig up the chest here. I'm sure you will need it.\
\
Farewell, $C. I pray we have no cause to meet again.",["O"]="Use the information you collected to seek Blackstone's treasure hoard.",["T"]="Into Purgatory",},[26329]={["D"]="Instead of treasure and the origin of the \"Veilbinder's\" curse, you find a note explaining that Blackstone hid the treasure elsewhere to protect his crew. This noble gesture condemns you to continue carrying the cursed Eye of Paleth.\
\
Only Blackstone's love knows the real location of the treasure. Finding her is your only hope to rid yourself of the curse.",["O"]="Find the mutual friend of Blackstone and his paramour. Maybe Blackstone's logs hold clues to where he had friends?",["T"]="Dreams of Another Life",},[26330]={["D"]="This farm was our dream. I think I always knew he would never actually make it back here. Being a privateer is hazardous work, and then when he turned to outright piracy....\
\
I have no idea how Blackstone managed to transport the treasure here, but he stowed it in a nearby cave. I suppose it was his last gift to me, but I haven't been able to access it. It is haunted by spirits from beyond the Veil. They will attempt to beat us back. But if you were strong enough to defeat my love in battle, and survive the curse to bring you here, perhaps you will be strong enough to defeat them.\
\
Let me know when you are ready to depart.",["O"]="Protect Para Grimtotem as she leads you to the treasure hoard.",["T"]="Dreams of Another Life",},[26331]={["D"]="Three moons ago our lookout spotted sails and ships on the horizon. He claimed he'd seen their banners before, but he seems too scared to recount where or with whom. Shortly after they were sighted, the sound of cannon fire echoed across the water.\
\
There is only one island in that direction: Tol Barad, home of the old Kirin Tor prison. What could someone want there? Is it a raid? An escape?\
\
I am curious and my superstitious crew is scared. You can help! Speak to Roost Master Hawkins and request a ride to Tol Barad. I need a scout to look at the isle and let me know what is going on.",["O"]="Take a Gryphon ride from Roost Master Hawkins and investigate the pirate assault on Tol Barad.",["T"]="Plundering Pirates",},[26332]={["D"]="Listen up! I've received from word from... well, let's just say an ally, claiming that a naval assault appears to be taking place at Tol Barad.\
\
That island ain't worth anything, so it is more than a little suspicious to receive this report.\
\
Head to Faldir's Cove and speak to Captain Steelgut and tell him I sent you. They'll know what it is about.",["O"]="Locate Captain Steelgut at Faldir's Cove within the Arathi Highlands.",["T"]="Plundering Pirates",},[26333]={["D"]="I can't swim and I certainly am not going to waste time learning now! What I need are the components to build my own boat - just a little thing, so I'm not asking for much here.\
\
Here's a list of components; run along now with that waterproof armor of yours and bring me this stuff. The sooner you go, the sooner you return, the sooner you get uncursed, and I get to sleep in a proper bed.\
\
Oh - where do you get that stuff? Well, I hear there's a lumbermill in Western Plaguelands, maybe you can acquire some there. Runecloth is just lying around where anyone can get it, right? Thread is sold by trade vendors and the Jugs of Pitch would come from other pirates.",["O"]="Get the supplies Winkey requested for building a ship and bring them to her island in Tanaris.",["T"]="My Kingdom for a Ship",},[26334]={["D"]="I can't build a ship with just my hands! I need the proper tools to assemble these components, and I need you to get them for me. Because I spent the intervening time since you were here last daydreaming about cheese and working on my tan, not learning to swim. It's important to have dreams! It keeps you going. And how many tan gnomes have you seen? My golden skin will create quite the stir.\
\
Anyway, I need a Blacksmith's Hammer, an Arclight Spanner, 50 Handfuls of Copper Bolts, and a Gnome-sized Jigsaw. A skilled engineer could help with some of those, but the Jigsaw only comes from one place - Gnomeregan!",["O"]="Get the tools Winkey needs to build herself a ship.",["T"]="My Kingdom for a Ship",},[26335]={["D"]="As I told you, my father gave his life to spare Blackstone and the rest of his orc crew from imprisonment. The orcs who sailed under my father were conscripted from the internment camps, and were remanded back to those camps after the Southshore privateer fleet was scuttled. My father petitioned for their freedom, but he was denied by Judge Thelgram and Overseer Lorin Remka. \
\
Thelgram has been dead for some time, but I believe Remka is still alive. If she had listened to reason, my father wouldn't have felt compelled to try to break the orcs out of the camp, and he wouldn't have died for the trouble. My conscience won't let me rest until she pays for his death, but I have no idea where she is now. \
\
Remka kept a female orc as a personal slave. Her name was Greekik. Remka also had an attaché at the camp named Waryk. I don't know if either of those people is still alive either, but if you can find either one, perhaps it will lead you to Remka's whereabouts.",["O"]="Determine if Lorin Remka is alive or dead.",["T"]="Stewel's Revenge",},[26336]={["D"]="I wish I could rely on the system of justice to mete out appropriate punishment, but there is little hope that the leaders of Stormwind will care about crimes committed in Lordaeron years before. \
\
My father would not have approved of my desire to avenge him. He even made me promise not to raise a hand against those fools, should the operation go wrong. There is a way I can keep the letter of that promise and my conscience will be clear. You must act as my hand of vengeance. If you do, I will tell you what you want to know.\
\
Lorin Remka must die. Blood shall pay for blood.",["O"]="Kill Lorin Remka.",["T"]="Stewel's Revenge",},[26337]={["D"]="Hail $C. If you've come looking for clandestine work, I can assure you that you're in the right place.\
\
I've heard there was a small breakout at the island prison of Baradin Hold. There are a couple prisoners incarcerated there that I really would prefer didn't escape. Both are powerful magic users who could wreck destruction on the Undercity. And we especially don't want any more necromancers running around.\
\
If you wouldn't mind taking a jaunt down to Faldir's Cove in the Arathi Highlands and hopping a flight to Tol Barad, I'll make it worth your while to make sure Astilos and Nazrasash never make it off the island.",["O"]="Enter Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad and kill Astilos the Hollow and Nazrasash.",["T"]="The Necromancer and the Scion",},[26338]={["D"]="As Grand Admiral of Stormwind's Navy, I receive reports about all sorts of incidents and skullduggery on the high seas. Recently, a disturbing report surfaced from the island stronghold of Tol Barad. Pirates may have overrun the old Kirin Tor prison.\
\
Right now this rumor is unsubstantiated. I need someone to head over to Tol Barad and assess the issue. You seem to be capable -- your Alliance needs you, adventurer.\
\
Stop in at SI:7 before you depart. They may have more information.",["O"]="Find someone in SI:7 who can give you more information about the current status of Baradin Hold.",["T"]="The Possible Fall of Baradin Hold",},[26339]={["D"]="The island of Tol Barad is home to the prison of Baradin Hold -- but Baradin isn't just any prison. Some of the worst creatures in the world were imprisoned there. There's even one that Kezan couldn't hold!\
\
So yeah, we gotta know if pirates have taken over the prison -- but if they have, we also have to do something about it. I'll leave it up to you to figure out the best course of action once you're on the ground there.\
\
Speaking of, if you don't know how to get there, you'll have to make a trip to Faldir's Cove in the Arathi Highlands. The flight master there will be happy to set you up.",["O"]="Investigate the situation at Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad to see if the rumors of a pirate attack are true.",["T"]="The Possible Fall of Baradin Hold",},[26340]={["D"]="Renzik instructed you to take matters into your own hands if you discovered the rumors were true.\
\
The simplest way to fix the situation is to take out the pirates who are currently controlling Baradin Hold.\
\
You'll need to fight your way through the prison to make sure order is restored.",["O"]="Kill the pirates responsible for assaulting Baradin Hold: Glagut, Calypso, and Pirate Lord Blackstone.",["T"]="The Possible Fall of Baradin Hold",},[26341]={["D"]="Hero of de Horde, your chieftains require your aid!\
\
De island of Tol Barad is home to de prison of Baradin Hold -- where some o' the worst beasties in de world were imprisoned. Dere's even one Kezan couldn't hold!\
\
Dere is a rumor dat pirates have taken over de prison. We need to investigate. I'll leave it to you to figure out de best course of action once you're on the ground there.\
\
Speaking of, if you don't know how to get there, you'll have to make a trip to Faldir's Cove in de Arathi Highlands. The flight master there will be happy to set you up.",["O"]="Investigate the situation at Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad to see if the rumors of a pirate attack are true.",["T"]="The Possible Fall of Baradin Hold",},[26342]={["D"]="Vol'jin instructed you to take matters into your own hands if you discovered the rumors were true.\
\
The simplest way to fix the situation is to take out the pirates who are currently controlling Baradin Hold.\
\
You'll need to fight your way through the prison to make sure order is restored.",["O"]="Kill the pirates responsible for assaulting Baradin Hold: Gluk, Calypso, and Pirate Lord Blackstone.",["T"]="The Possible Fall of Baradin Hold",},[26343]={["D"]="Hail $C. If you've come looking for clandestine work, I can assure you that you're in the right place.\
\
I've heard there was a small breakout at the island prison of Baradin Hold. There are a couple prisoners incarcerated there that I really would prefer didn't escape. There's a decent chance they'd come looking for me and I don't want that kind of chaos in Stormwind.\
\
If you wouldn't mind taking a jaunt down to Faldir's Cove in the Arathi Highlands and hopping a flight to Tol Barad, I'll make it worth your while to make sure Morrumus and Dak'mal never make it off the island.",["O"]="Enter Baradin Hold on the island of Tol Barad and kill Morrumus and Dak'mal.",["T"]="To All the Demons I Used to Love",},[26344]={["D"]="I suspect you're looking for the rest of the treasure haul that the orb came from and I have good news - it was buried wholesale near where we captured the vessel. The bad news is, I only have part of the location. Blackstone split the coordinates between me, Winks and Junior. So you'll have to talk to them to get the rest of the info.\
\
But first - I've been having a little problem with a rival cartel member. Since leaving the Blackstone crew, I've been freelancing for the Blackwater Raiders and I've locked triggers with Boss Oglethorpe from the Venture Company on more than one occasion. I'm tired of having to watch my back every time I step foot outside Booty Bay. Take her out for me, and I'll tell you what you want to know. \
\
She's got a little base somewhere here in Stranglethorn but I don't know where it is.",["O"]="Locate Boss Oglethorpe in Stranglethorn Vale and eliminate her.",["T"]="You Scratch My Back...",},[26345]={["D"]="I have great news, $N! The Explorer's League were able to decipher some of the runes on the Discs of Norgannon. Strangely, they're similar to runes used in the ancient Taurahe language.\
\
We were able to find a tauren contact willing to work with us to decipher the runes and we'd like you to work with her. She agreed to travel from Thunder Bluff to Ratchet to meet you. Meet Kaletaka Winterbluff at the inn there, and we'll be one step closer to opening Uldum!",["O"]="Meet Kaletaka Winterbluff in Ratchet to discuss the Discs of Norgannon.",["T"]="The Good News",},[26346]={["D"]="Awhile ago the Explorer's League was given an artifact called the Discs of Norgannon. We've been trying to glean some information from the Discs, and to proceed, we need a specialist in the Taurahe language.\
\
We were able to find a tauren contact willing to work with us and we need a courier to meet with her. I've heard you recommended around town, so I'd like you to meet Kaletaka Winterbluff at the Broken Keel Tavern in Ratchet. If we're right, these Discs could lead to opening the ancient facility of Uldum!",["O"]="Meet Kaletaka Winterbluff in Ratchet to discuss the Discs of Norgannon.",["T"]="An Exciting Discovery",},[26347]={["D"]="I'll be honest, it's a little nerve-wracking meeting a $R face to face, but my mother wasn't one to let faction grievances get in the way of the pursuit of knowledge.\
\
She was concerned on the trip here though because she thought someone shady was following us. She decided not to wait here, and wanted me to tell you she was headed to Felwood. Since she was on foot, I'm sure you can catch up to her.\
\
I'm worried about her, $R, but I'm sure my mom can take care of herself.",["O"]="Find Kaletaka Winterbluff somewhere on the road between Ratchet and Felwood.",["T"]="The Good News",},[26348]={["D"]="Kaletaka Winterbluff's body has been looted of all valuables. She appears to have been ambushed as there are no defensive marks on her hands. A single cut, right across the throat, speaks to the efficiency of her killer.\
\
You are about to leave when you spy a single strange hoofprint in the mud nearby. You memorize the details of that hoofprint, knowing you must return to Mulin Winterbluff in Ratchet and tell him that his mother's suspicion she was being followed appears correct -- to everyone's detriment.",["O"]="Return to Mulin Winterbluff in Ratchet with the bad news.",["T"]="The Bad News",},[26349]={["D"]="<As Mulin works to calm himself, you describe the hoofprint you saw in the mud.>\
\
I wish I could help you but I can't concentrate right now. But before you leave, there is something my mother gave me that you should have, $R.\
\
My mom told me that if something did happen to her to give you this note. I hope it helps with whatever you needed her for.\
\
Forgive me if I say I never want to see another $R again.",["O"]="Take Kaletaka's Encrypted Note to High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge.",["T"]="The Bad News",},[26350]={["D"]="I will work on decoding Kaletaka's message, but while you were gone some of the other members of the Explorer's League made a break-through in deciphering the location of the Plates of Uldum.\
\
Speak to Historian Karnik if you'd like to learn more.",["O"]="Speak to Historian Karnik at the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge.",["T"]="The Good News Again",},[26351]={["D"]="The Explorer's League have deciphered a couple of pieces of information that indicate the Plates of Uldum were kept somewhere that has persistent smoke. Also, the words for \"gorge\" and \"cave\" seem to appear frequently.\
\
It would seem obvious that Searing Gorge is mentioned, but remember, these discs were created long before Ragnaros was summoned. Searing Gorge didn't exist then.\
\
But Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring did.\
\
We'd like you to use your considerable talents to search Darkwhisper Gorge for any sign of the Plates of Uldum. Report back with anything you find.",["O"]="Search Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring for a clue to the location of the Plates of Uldum.",["T"]="The Good News Again",},[26352]={["D"]="I know what you seek and I have seen the valiance with which you seek it. Rest assured, I do not say this lightly, for I have seen how much mortals will sacrifice for the pursuit of knowledge.\
\
Be warned, you are not ready for the Plates of Uldum. You are not ready for what waits behind those doors. Even the Titans weren't ready for what they found, which is why the Plates and Discs were separated and scattered to the winds.\
\
If you continue to follow this trail, it will unleash unspeakable doom. Go now, $R. This quest is at an end. I urge you to find a new one.",["O"]="Return to Historian Karnik in Ironforge with the Earthcaller's message.",["T"]="The Bad News Again",},[26353]={["D"]="I have great news, $N! The Lorespeakers were able to decipher some of the runes on the Discs of Norgannon. They're written in the ancient dwarven language.\
\
We were able to find a dwarven contact willing to work with us to decipher the runes and we'd like you to meet with him. He agreed to travel from Ironforge to Ratchet to meet with you. Meet Hedrig Ironstone at the inn there, and we'll be one step closer to opening Uldum!",["O"]="Meet Hedrig Ironstone in Booty Bay to discuss the Discs of Norgannon.",["T"]="The Good News",},[26354]={["D"]="Awhile ago the Lorespeakers were given an artifact called the Discs of Norgannon. We've been trying to glean some information from the Discs and to proceed, we need a specialist in the dwarven language.\
\
We were able to find a dwarf contact willing to work with us and we need a courier to meet with him. I've heard you recommended around town, so I'd like you to meet Hedrig Ironstone at the Broken Keel Tavern in Ratchet. If we're right, these Discs could lead to opening the ancient facility of Uldum!",["O"]="Meet Hedrig Ironstone in Ratchet to discuss the Discs of Norgannon.",["T"]="An Exciting Discovery",},[26355]={["D"]="I'll be honest, it's a little nerve-wrackin' meetin' a $R face to face, but Da wasn't one to let faction greivances get in the way of the pursuit of knowledge.\
\
He was concerned on the trip here though. Thought someone was watchin' and followin' us, so he set out on his own. He wanted me to tell you he was headed to Felwood. Since he was on foot, I'm sure ya can catch up to 'im.\
\
I'm worried about 'im, $R, but I'm sure my Da can take care of 'imself.",["O"]="Find Hedrig Ironstone somewhere on the road between Ratchet and Felwood.",["T"]="The Good News",},[26356]={["D"]="Hedrig Ironstone's body has been looted of all valuables. He appears to have been ambushed as there are no defensive marks on his hands. A single cut, right across the throat, speaks to the efficiency of his killer.\
\
You are about to leave when you spy a single footprint in the mud nearby. You memorize the details of that footprint, knowing you must return to Nelly Ironstone in Ratchet and tell her that her father's suspicion he was being followed appears correct -- to everyone's detriment.",["O"]="Return to Nelly Ironstone in Ratchet with the bad news.",["T"]="The Bad News",},[26357]={["D"]="<As Nelly works to calm herself, you describe the footprint you saw in the mud.>\
\
I wish I could help you but that strange shoe tread doesn't sound familiar to me. But there is something, $R.\
\
My Da told me that if somethin' did happen to 'im to give you this note. I hope it helps with whatever you needed my Da for.\
\
Forgive me if I say I never want to see another $R again.",["O"]="Take Hedrig's Encrypted Message to Sage Truthseeker in Thunder Bluff.",["T"]="The Bad News",},[26358]={["D"]="I will work on decoding Hedrig's message, but while you were gone some of the other Lorespeakers believe they'd made a break-through in deciphering the location of the Plates of Uldum.\
\
Speak to Sage Nasha on the Spirit Rise if you'd like to learn more.",["O"]="Speak to Sage Nasha on the Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff.",["T"]="The Good News Again",},[26359]={["D"]="The Lorespeakers have deciphered a couple of pieces of information that indicate the Plates of Uldum were kept somewhere that has persistent smoke. Also, the words for \"gorge\" and \"cave\" seem to appear frequently.\
\
It would seem obvious that Searing Gorge is mentioned, but remember, these discs were created long before Ragnaros was summoned. Searing Gorge didn't exist then.\
\
But Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring did.\
\
We'd like you to use your considerable talents to search Darkwhisper Gorge for any sign of the Plates of Uldum. Report back with anything you find.",["O"]="Search Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring for a clue to the location of the Plates of Uldum.",["T"]="The Good News Again",},[26360]={["D"]="I know what you seek and I have seen the valiance with which you seek it. Rest assured, I do not say this lightly, for I have seen how much mortals will sacrifice for the pursuit of knowledge.\
\
Be warned: you are not ready for the Plates of Uldum. You are not ready for what waits behind those doors. Even the Titans weren't ready for what they found, which is why the Plates and Discs were separated and scattered to the winds.\
\
If you continue to follow this trail, it will unleash unspeakable doom. Go now, $R. This quest is at an end. I urge you to find a new one.",["O"]="Return to Sage Nasha in Thunder Bluff with the Earthcaller's message.",["T"]="The Bad News Again",},[26361]={["D"]="Stonetalon Mountains belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Stonetalon Mountains locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Stonetalon Mountains",},[26362]={["D"]="Stonetalon Mountains belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Stonetalon Mountains locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Stonetalon Mountains",},[26363]={["D"]="Ashenvale belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Ashenvale locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Ashenvale",},[26364]={["D"]="Ashenvale belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Ashenvale locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Ashenvale",},[26365]={["D"]="Hillsbrad Foothills belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Hillsbrad Foothills locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Hillsbrad Foothills",},[26366]={["D"]="Hillsbrad Foothills belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Hillsbrad Foothills locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Hillsbrad Foothills",},[26367]={["D"]="Thousand Needles belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Thousand Needles locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Thousand Needles",},[26368]={["D"]="Thousand Needles belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Thousand Needles locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Thousand Needles",},[26369]={["D"]="Alterac Mountains belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Alterac Mountains locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Alterac Mountains",},[26370]={["D"]="Alterac Mountains belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Alterac Mountains locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Alterac Mountains",},[26371]={["D"]="Desolace belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Desolace locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Desolace",},[26372]={["D"]="Desolace belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Desolace locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Desolace",},[26373]={["D"]="Arathi Highlands belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Arathi Highlands locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Arathi Highlands",},[26374]={["D"]="Arathi Highlands belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Arathi Highlands locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Arathi Highlands",},[26375]={["D"]="Swamp of Sorrows belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Swamp of Sorrows locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Swamp of Sorrows",},[26376]={["D"]="Swamp of Sorrows belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Swamp of Sorrows locate and slay 5 members of the Alliance.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Swamp of Sorrows",},[26377]={["D"]="Badlands belongs to the Alliance and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Horde and slay them on behalf of the army to prove your worth and rise through the ranks.",["O"]="Within Badlands locate and slay 5 members of the Horde.",["T"]="Call to Skirmish: Badlands",},[26378]={["D"]="Badlands belongs to the Horde and we must constantly demonstrate this. Hunt down members of the Alliance and slay them on behalf of the army to prove yo